        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "51047e35-d358-50c5-95a1-28490c01583f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Brent Bennett, Jonathan Idema, Osama Bin Laden\n- Places: Kabul, Afghanistan\n- Roles: former US Army paratrooper, independent security contractors, covert operatives, special forces operative\n- Organizations: Afghan court, US government, US military, Taliban\n- Concepts: torture, kidnapping, private jail, media misrepresentation\n\nFacts:\n- On 15 September 2004, an Afghan court convicted Brent Bennett for participating in torture and kidnapping and for running a private jail in Kabul.\n- Brent Bennett was a former US Army paratrooper.\n- In Afghanistan, Brent Bennett and Jonathan Idema operated as independent security contractors.\n- Brent Bennett and Jonathan Idema represented themselves to the American and international media, members of the US military, and Afghan nationals as US government-sponsored covert operatives.\n- Brent Bennett and Jonathan Idema claimed they were tracking and apprehending Osama Bin Laden and senior Taliban officials.\n- At the same time, Jonathan Idema portrayed himself as a U.S. government-sponsored special forces operative on a mission to apprehend terrorists.\n- The U.S. government repeatedly denied most of Jonathan Idema's claims.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "fb78cb87-0644-50f1-a314-ae258a7237be",
        "text": "Page: Brent Bennett. Sentence: Brent Bennett is a former US Army paratrooper who was convicted by an Afghan court on 15 September 2004 for participating in torture and kidnapping, and for running a private jail in Kabul.\nPage: Brent Bennett. Sentence: Bennett and his associate Jonathan Idema had been operating as independent security contractors in Afghanistan, but had been representing themselves to the American and international media, members of the US military, and Afghan nationals as US government-sponsored covert operatives to track and apprehend Osama Bin Laden and senior Taliban officials.\nPage: Jonathan Idema. Sentence: At the time, Idema had been portraying himself as a U.S. government-sponsored special forces operative on a mission to apprehend terrorists. However, the U.S. government has repeatedly denied most of such claims.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
